Public baseline: atyrode/code v0.19.0
Commit: 23f89adec1ff4b3b85018d4c77a38b79de227bad

Downstream continuity-bridge patch only; not a new Go/native Code product.
Route native shared roles without named-agent overrides; retain explicit dials,
account pools, independent task settings, and utility effort boundaries.
Routine intent survives unrelated saves/restarts and skips only known-down main
quota. Legacy lane/model maps stay explicit. Local utilities respect the honest
local effort ceiling; hosted memory remains cheap medium. Widget and memory each
have an explicit empty chain; backend/enabled/autolearn preferences are untouched.
Refresh exact-identity metadata without paid probes or new entitlements.
Retain authoritative standard windows independently of authored capability tiers;
do not infer extended windows or reject smaller windows on premium rungs.
Tests render authored input fixtures and assert parsed consumer contracts, not
copied generated-output snapshots. The obsolete snapshot file is removed by the
package's explicit postPatch step, without reproducing its generated rows here.

